<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fruela I of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 722–<a href="/years/768">768</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fruela I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 757 to 768, the son of Alfonso I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ermesinda">Ermesinda</a>. He fought the Muslims of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> and put down revolts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> and among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basques">Basques</a>, and married the Basque captive Munia, mother of Alfonso II. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oviedo">Oviedo</a> around 761, which later became the royal capital. He was murdered in 768 by members of his own court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fruela-i-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Fruela I of Asturias" width="320" height="549" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Froila_I_no_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
